---
title: Homemade Cheeseburger Macaroni
servings: 4
cuisine: american
main_protein: beef
prep_time: "5 minutes"
cook_time: "20 minutes"
tags:
  - dinner
  - beef
  - macaroni
  - cheese
source: https://www.spendwithpennies.com/cheeseburger-macaroni-stove-top-youll-never-buy-the-boxed-kind-again/
image: ../obsidian/attachments/cheeseburger-macaroni.jpg
prep:
  - Finely dice 0.5 cup onion
  - Mix the cornstarch and spices in a small bowl
  - Shred 1.75 cups sharp cheddar cheese
---

Combine @cornstarch{1%tablespoon}, @garlic powder{2%teaspoons}, @granulated sugar{1%teaspoon}, @salt{1%teaspoon}, @paprika{1%teaspoon}, and @black pepper{0.5%teaspoon} in a #small bowl{}; set aside.

Brown @lean ground beef{1%pound} and @onion{0.5%cup}, finely diced (or 1 teaspoon onion powder), in a #large skillet{} over medium-high heat, breaking it apart with a #wooden spoon{} until fully cooked. Drain excess fat.

Add @milk{2%cups}, @chicken broth{1.25%cup}, and uncooked @elbow macaroni{1.5%cups} to the beef. Stir in the spice mixture. Bring to a boil over medium-high heat.

Once boiling, reduce heat to a gentle boil, cover, and simmer ~{9%minutes} to 12 minutes until pasta is tender, stirring occasionally. Add more broth or water if needed.

Remove from heat and stir in @sharp cheddar cheese{1.75%cups}, shredded, until completely melted. Serve immediately.
